well through the covet pandemic many of  us have faced our own personal  challenges  overcoming them can be challenging and  it really requires resiliency  and brian someone well qualified to talk  about resiliency is jim davidson  the mountain climber summited mount  everest in 2017  two years after he was nearly killed in  an earthquake on the mountain  well his story is one of survival  followed by success  in some pretty tough circumstances  here's his first-hand account from that  2015 earthquake all of a sudden  the glacier jerked into the air and  lifted the tent up and then we dropped  back down  and then we went back up again as the  waves rippled through the glacier and  being in the tent was like being in a  life raft out on the ocean and that's  when i knew it was an earthquake  and when that happened we could hear the  roar of avalanches we're having an  earthquake all at once  it was pure survival mode for a good  couple of minutes  after surviving that earthquake jim and  his team were rescued from mount everest  they then spent the remainder of their  adventure helping those in nepal who'd  lost  everything clean up and begin the  rebuilding process  but two years later jim returned to  mount everest to try again this time  he made it jim says while you may not be  a mountain climber  we all have our own personal everest and  many of the tools he used to overcome  his challenges  can be used by all of us to help  overcome ours  whether it's an earthquake recovery or a  pandemic or an economic crisis  you help them they help you somebody  else helps and we're all slowly lifting  each other up and we'll have bad days  when someone stumbles and that's when  someone needs to lift them up again  as you move forward through life you  might have a big aspiration but things  are going to go sideways  there's going to be earthquakes there's  going to be pandemics so how can you be  resilient enough to endure the bad  things when they're happening  try and grow from it and re-engage with  the next set of challenges  the next opportunity the next everest  so jim has a recounted both of his  everest experiences and detailed how we  can all use resiliency to survive  challenges  he's got a new book it is titled there  it is the next everest  you can read it now and watch an  extended interview with jim just head to  our website at 8newsnow.com and  click on the everest story for all of  those inspiring details guys
 

